<title>CANADA: Canada dollar ends firmer after Thiessen comments.</title>
<headline>Canada dollar ends firmer after Thiessen comments.</headline>
<text>
<p>FORECAST RANGE   1.3910/1.3950	    ASIAN CLOSE     1.3955</p>
<p>RESISTANCE 1.3910   SUPPORT 1.3970	HI 1.3956   LO  1.3930</p>
<p>CANADA OPEN  1.3930/40    HI 1.3942     EUROPE OPEN     1.3940</p>
<p>PREV CLOSE   1.3952/57    LO 1.3910     HI 1.3948   LO  1.3929</p>
<p>----------------------MARKET COMMENT--------------------------</p>
<p>* The Canadian dollar ended firmer on Wednesday around C$1.3935 (US$0.7176) from Tuesday's close of C$1.3952 (US$0.7167) * Bank of Canada Governor Gordon Thiessen said economic fundamentals pointed to upward trend in Canadian dollar * Thiessen said Canada would see solid economic expansion in 1997 * He added Canada could not have completely independent interest rate policy</p>
</text>
